| | **Atsugi City Zoo & Botanical Garden** | • 200+ animal species, a reptile house, and a tropical greenhouse. | • Mon‑Fri 9 – 17 h, Sat 9 – 17 h, Sun 9 – 17 h. <br>• Admission ¥500 (children < 6 free). <br>• 20‑min bus ride (Atsugi City Bus 12). | Perfect for families and a gentle introduction to wildlife. |
| **Yokohama** | **Yokohama Chinatown** | • Largest Chinatown in Japan, 200+ restaurants & shops. <br>• Lantern‑lit streets, the iconic “Chinatown Gate.” | • Open 24 h. <br>• Free to wander; dining costs vary. <br>• 30‑min train (JR or Keikyu) from Atsugi Station. | A vibrant, colorful culinary adventure. |
| | **Yokohama Red Brick Warehouse** | • Historic warehouses turned into a shopping & event complex. <br>• Seasonal markets, art exhibitions, and rooftop garden. | • Mon‑Fri 10 – 18 h, Sat 10 – 18 h, Sun 10 – 18 h. <br>• Admission free (shops & events vary). <br>• 35‑min train + 10‑min walk. | A blend of history, culture, and modern retail. |
| | **Yamashita Park & Yamashita Pier** | • Seaside promenade, flower gardens, and the iconic “Yamashita Pier.” <br>• Great spot for sunset views. | • Open 24 h. <br>• Free. <br>• 30‑min train + 5‑min walk. | Ideal for a relaxed stroll with scenic views. |
