| | **Great Buddha (Daibutsu) – Kotoku-in** | • 13.35 m bronze statue, one of Japan’s largest. <br>• Surrounding gardens and a small museum. | • Mon‑Fri 9 – 17 h, Sat 9 – 17 h, Sun 9 – 17 h. <br>• Admission ¥200 (free for children < 6). <br>• 45‑min train + 15‑min walk. | Iconic landmark that’s both awe‑inspiring and accessible. |
| | **Hasedera Temple** | • 8‑story pagoda, beautiful gardens, and the “Kannon” statue. | • Mon‑Fri 9 – 17 h, Sat 9 – 17 h, Sun 9 – 17 h. <br>• Admission ¥200 (free for children < 6). <br>• 45‑min train + 20‑min walk. | Stunning architecture and serene gardens. |
| **Fujisawa** | **Enoshima Island** | • Small island with caves, a lighthouse, and a shrine. <br>• Enoshima Sea Candle (lighthouse‑like observation tower). | • Open 24 h. <br>• Free (some attractions charge). <br>• 30‑min train + 10‑min walk. | Beautiful coastal scenery and fun for all ages. |
| | **Fujisawa Beach** | • Long sandy beach, ideal for sunbathing and beach sports. | • Open 24 h. <br>• Free. <br>• 30‑min train + 5‑min walk. | Great spot for a quick beach escape. |
